# Saved articles (phase 3): saved articles stay when their feed is unpinned; the page lists them newest saved first,
# each with its feed, when it was saved and its size, and a line at the bottom (how many, how much of the cap); the options
# by a 3 s hold or Ctrl+O: Article info (when it was saved, its size), Remove from saved (asked first: Cancel keeps it);
# the one left opens in the reader from its copy. (No first-run hint here: the options of Favorites were opened first.)
seed pin us-ars-technica
seed refresh
seed save us-ars-technica 1
seed save us-ars-technica 4
seed refresh_on_open off
wait 900
key enter
wait 500
expect state page favorites
key ctrl-o
wait 400
tap "Unpin"
wait 400
expect state popup confirm
tap "Unpin"
wait 600
expect state subs 0
key esc
wait 300
key down
key down
key enter
wait 500
expect state page saved
expect state saved 2
expect text "^2 articles, "
shot 01-saved
check saved
hold "^What the new memory" 3400
wait 400
expect state popup menu
expect text "Remove from saved"
expect text "Article info"
shot 02-options
check saved-options
tap "Article info"
wait 400
expect state popup info
expect text "^Saved "
shot 03-info
check saved-info
key enter
wait 300
expect notext "Hold or press Ctrl+O for options"
key ctrl-o
wait 400
tap "Remove from saved"
wait 400
expect state popup confirm
tap "Cancel"
wait 300
expect state saved 2
key ctrl-o
wait 400
tap "Remove from saved"
wait 400
tap "Remove"
wait 500
expect state saved 1
expect text "Removed from saved"
expect text "^1 article, "
shot 04-removed-one
key home
key enter
wait 800
expect state page reader
expect state is_saved 1
expect text "New Linux kernel fixes the long-standing scheduler stall on small boards"
shot 05-reader-saved
